tivates the dive reflex and rapidly calms your nervous system."}, {"skill": "🏃 I — Intense Exercise", "description": "Do 20 jumping jacks, run in place, or do any intense physical activity for a few minutes. Exercise burns off stress hormones and shifts emotional energy."}, {"skill": "🫁 P — Paced Breathing", "description": "Breathe in for 4 counts, out for 6 counts. Make your exhale longer than your inhale to activate the parasympathetic nervous system and reduce heart rate."}, {"skill": "💪 P — Progressive Relaxation", "description": "Tense each muscle group for 5 seconds then release: feet → calves → thighs → stomach → hands → arms → shoulders → face. Notice the difference between tension and relaxation."}]}, {"id": 7, "title": "ACCEPTS", "subtitle": "Distraction Skills", "category": "DBT", "icon": "🎭", "color": "#BE185D", "duration": "5–30 min", "type": "dbt", "description": "Use purposeful distraction to tolerate distress without making it worse.", "dbtSkills": [{"skill": "🎨 A — Activities", "description": "Engage in any activity that occupies your mind: exercise, cleaning, gaming, crafts, cooking. The goal is to fully focus on something else."}, {"skill": "❤️ C — Contributing", "description": "Do something for someone else: send a kind message, volunteer, help a neighbor. Focusing outward breaks the cycle of rumination."}, {"skill": "⚖️ C — Comparisons", "description": "Compare your situation to a time when things were harder, or to others facing greater challenges. This is not minimizing — it is gaining perspective."}, {"skill": "😂 E — Emotions (Opposite)", "description": "Generate an emotion opposite to the distressing one: watch a funny video, read something uplifting, listen to energizing music."}, {"skill": "🚗 P — Pushing Away", "description": "Temporarily push the situation out of your mind. Imagine placing it in a box on a shelf. Give yourself permission to deal with it later."}, {"skill": "🧠 T — Thoughts", "description": "Redirect your thoughts: count backwards from 100 by 7s, recite song lyrics, name all the countries you know, do a word puzzle."}, {"skill": "🌶️ S — Sensations", "description": "Use intense sensations to shift focus: hold ice, snap a rubber band, chew something sour, do cold water immersion."}]}, {"id": 8, "title": "DEAR MAN", "subtitle": "Interpersonal Effectiveness", "category": "DBT", "icon": "💬", "color": "#00897B", "duration": "10–15 min", "type": "worksheet", "description": "Communicate your needs effectively while maintaining relationships and self-respect.", "worksheetFields": [{"key": "situation", "label": "What Do You Need to Ask For or Say?", "placeholder": "Briefly describe the situation...", "multiline": true}, {"key": "describe", "label": "D — Describe the Facts", "placeholder": "Stick to the observable facts, no judgments...", "multiline": true}, {"key": "express", "label": "E — Express How You Feel", "description": "Use \"I feel...\" statements", "placeholder": "\"I feel ____ when ____ because ____...\"", "multiline": false}, {"key": "assert", "label": "A — Assert What You Want", "placeholder": "Ask for what you need clearly and directly...", "multiline": false}, {"key": "reinforce", "label": "R — Reinforce (Show Benefits)", "placeholder": "How will this benefit both of you?", "multiline": true}, {"key": "keep_mindful", "label": "M — Stay Mindful (What is your goal?)", "placeholder": "Focus on your objective. What do you want from this interaction?", "multiline": false}, {"key": "appear", "label": "A — Appear Confident (How will you do this?)", "placeholder": "Describe your body language, tone, eye contact...", "multiline": false}, {"key": "negotiate", "label": "N — Negotiate (What are you willing to compromise on?)", "placeholder": "What could you offer or accept?", "multiline": true}]}, {"id": 9, "title": "Opposite Action", "subtitle": "Emotion Regulation", "category": "DBT", "icon": "🔄", "color": "#7C3AED", "duration": "5–10 min", "type": "worksheet", "description": "Change an un