now about this situation?\"\n3. Breathe in \"Wise,\" breathe out \"Mind.\"\n4. Let the answer arise from within — not forced, not dismissed.\n5. Trust it."}]}, {"id": 11, "title": "IMPROVE the Moment", "subtitle": "Distress Tolerance", "category": "DBT", "icon": "✨", "color": "#E8673A", "duration": "10–20 min", "type": "dbt", "description": "Strategies to make a painful moment more bearable without making it worse.", "dbtSkills": [{"skill": "🙏 I — Imagery", "description": "Imagine a safe, peaceful place in vivid detail. What does it look, sound, smell, feel like? Spend 2–3 minutes there."}, {"skill": "💡 M — Meaning", "description": "Find or create meaning in the situation. Ask: \"What can I learn from this? How might this make me stronger?\""}, {"skill": "🙌 P — Prayer / Spirituality", "description": "Connect to something larger than yourself — nature, spirituality, the universe, or your deepest values."}, {"skill": "😌 R — Relaxation", "description": "Do one relaxation activity: progressive muscle relaxation, deep breathing, warm bath, soft music."}, {"skill": "🌟 O — One Thing at a Time", "description": "Focus entirely on what you are doing right now. Notice when your mind wanders and gently bring it back."}, {"skill": "🏖️ V — Vacation", "description": "Give yourself a brief mental or physical vacation: a 30-minute break, a treat, doing something purely enjoyable."}, {"skill": "💪 E — Encouragement", "description": "Be your own cheerleader. Say: \"I can get through this.\" \"This feeling will pass.\" \"I have survived hard things before.\""}]}, {"id": 12, "title": "4-7-8 Breathing", "subtitle": "Anxiety Relief", "category": "Mindfulness", "icon": "🌬️", "color": "#00897B", "duration": "4 min", "type": "breathing", "description": "A breathing technique that activates the parasympathetic nervous system to calm anxiety.", "breathPattern": [{"phase": "Breathe In", "seconds": 4, "color": "#5C2D91"}, {"phase": "Hold", "seconds": 7, "color": "#D4A017"}, {"phase": "Breathe Out", "seconds": 8, "color": "#00897B"}]}, {"id": 13, "title": "Box Breathing", "subtitle": "Stress & Focus", "category": "Mindfulness", "icon": "⬛", "color": "#0891B2", "duration": "4 min", "type": "breathing", "description": "Used by Navy SEALs for stress control. Equal intervals create a sense of balance and control.", "breathPattern": [{"phase": "Breathe In", "seconds": 4, "color": "#5C2D91"}, {"phase": "Hold", "seconds": 4, "color": "#D4A017"}, {"phase": "Breathe Out", "seconds": 4, "color": "#00897B"}, {"phase": "Hold", "seconds": 4, "color": "#E8673A"}]}, {"id": 14, "title": "5-4-3-2-1 Grounding", "subtitle": "Sensory Awareness", "category": "Mindfulness", "icon": "🌍", "color": "#7C3AED", "duration": "5 min", "type": "guided", "description": "Use your five senses to anchor yourself in the present moment and reduce anxiety.", "steps": ["👁️ Name 5 things you can SEE right now.\nLook around slowly. Notice colors, shapes, textures, light.", "✋ Name 4 things you can TOUCH or feel.\nFeel the chair under you, clothes on your skin, floor under your feet.", "👂 Name 3 things you can HEAR.\nClose your eyes. Listen for sounds near and far.", "👃 Name 2 things you can SMELL.\nBreath in through your nose. If you can't smell much, think of 2 favorite scents.", "👅 Name 1 thing you can TASTE.\nNotice any taste in your mouth. If nothing, think of your favorite food.", "🌟 Take 3 slow breaths.\nIn through your nose, out through your mouth. Notice how you feel now."]}, {"id": 15, "title": "Body Scan", "subtitle": "Progressive Relaxation", "category": "Mindfulness", "icon": "🧘", "color": "#5C2D91", "duration": "10 min", "type": "guided", "description": "Systematically bring awareness through your body to release tension and build mindfulness.", "steps": ["🪑 Get comfortable.\nSit or lie down. Close your eyes. Take 3 slow breaths to settle in.", "🦶 Bring awareness to your feet.\nNotice any sensations — warmth, coolness, tingling, pressure. No need to change anything.", "🦵 Move attention